      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C2"],
      "pins": ["C2.1", "C2.2"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "GND"],
      "observed": "C2 is 100nF on the +5V output of the LM1117-5.0 regulator.",
      "expected": "The LM1117 datasheet requires a minimum output capacitance of 10uF (tantalum or aluminum) for stability; 100nF is far too small.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "C2 | 100nF | Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric | Device:C_Small"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "+5V : C2.1(passive) ... U1.2(VO,power_out)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The 5V regulator may oscillate or be unstable, causing unreliable operation of the MCUs and logic.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain two anomalies: the 4-pin fan connector's PWM pin is tied to GND, and the LM1117-5.0 regulator's output capacitor is only 100nF instead of the required 10uF. Both can cause the board to behave differently from intended."
}

